{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:LiftingAndDescent.BraneBoundary","@type":"LeanModule","name":"LiftingAndDescent.BraneBoundary","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Submodule.Ker"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.braneBoundary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.braneBoundary","kind":"def","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/brane-boundary.lean#L20-L30","doc":"The defining boundary of the n-th brane: the submodule consisting\nof elements that are \"new\" at level n (not descended from level n-1).\n\nCategorically: ∂Aₙ = {S ↪ Aₙ | ker(rₙ|_S) ≠ 0}\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:brane-boundary}` ","signatureChunk":0}]}